      {"t":"mc","q":"How do you ask 'Do you have time?' (to a stranger)","o":["Máte čas?","Děláte mít čas?","Máte ne čas?","Je máte čas?"],"why":"Keep the statement as it is and raise your voice: Czech has no word for do."},
      {"t":"mc","q":"Which question is for a friend, not a stranger?","o":["Máš čas?","Máte čas?","Mám čas?","Nemáte čas?"],"why":"máš is the ty form. Recognize it, and say máte to a stranger."},
      {"t":"order","p":"I don't speak Czech. (start with the verb)","a":["Nemluvím","česky"],"x":["Nemluvíte"],"why":"Nemluvím is the I-form with ne- in front: the verb ending -ím stays."},
      {"t":"order","p":"We are not from Prague. (start with the verb)","a":["Nejsme","z","Prahy"],"x":["Nejsou"],"why":"Nejsme is the we-form of být with ne- in front."},
      {"t":"order","p":"That isn't beer. (start with To)","a":["To","není","pivo"],"x":["neje"],"why":"je becomes není: the negative on-form of být."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Máte čas? Ne, __.","p":"Do you have time? No, I don't.","a":["nemám"],"o":["nemáte","mám","ne mám"],"why":"Answer with the I-form and ne- written on the verb: nemám."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"To __ káva.","p":"That isn't coffee.","a":["není"],"o":["neje","nejsem","nejste"],"why":"The negative of je is není."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Nemám __.","p":"I don't have anything.","a":["nic"],"o":["něco","ne","to"],"why":"Czech keeps ne- on the verb and adds nic: two negatives are normal."},
      {"t":"type","p":"I'm not a student. (a man)","a":["Nejsem student.","Já nejsem student.","Student nejsem."],"hint":"být · student · ne- joins the verb","x":["Nejste"],"why":"Nejsem is the I-form of být with ne- in front."},
      {"t":"type","p":"Do you speak English? (to a stranger)","a":["Mluvíte anglicky?","Vy mluvíte anglicky?"],"hint":"mluvit · anglicky · no word for do","x":["Mluvíš"],"why":"Mluvíte is the vy-form: the verb ending -íte, and nothing is added for do."},
      {"t":"type","p":"I don't have time.","a":["Nemám čas.","Já nemám čas.","Čas nemám."],"hint":"mít · čas","x":["Nemáte"],"why":"Nemám is the I-form: ne- plus mám, written as one word."}
